00:19:59,180 --> 00:20:01,600
Oh, so you still want to fight?

255
00:20:01,920 --> 00:20:04,861
It would appear pig-headedness
runs in the family.

256
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:06,860
How ungrateful can you be?

257
00:20:07,100 --> 00:20:09,937
You're blatantly ignoring
your grandfather's wishes,

258
00:20:10,020 --> 00:20:13,877
even after he gave his life to tell
you about the power of the world.

259
00:20:13,960 --> 00:20:17,431
Surely his pathetic pleas
warranted a bit of consideration.

260
00:20:17,520 --> 00:20:22,020
I have to move closer if I want to
beat your sorry ass to a pulp. Really?

261
00:20:23,140 --> 00:20:24,120
Okay, then.

262
00:20:24,260 --> 00:20:26,020
By all means, come closer.

263
00:20:36,460 --> 00:20:41,837
you'll have to be faster my stand
is more powerful than any other even

264
00:20:41,920 --> 00:20:45,577
without the world's tremendous power
and speed it would still outclass

265
00:20:45,660 --> 00:20:49,957
your pitiful star platinum your stand
has a lot in common with my star

266
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:54,340
platinum we're not long-range
fighters but we have incredible power

267
00:20:55,020 --> 00:20:56,460
If I'm being honest,

268
00:20:56,680 --> 00:20:58,497
I've always had a desire to see how much

269
00:20:58,580 --> 00:21:01,521
stronger the world is
compared with Star Platinum.

270
00:21:01,940 --> 00:21:05,100
But it seems pointless
to compare them now.

271
00:21:05,360 --> 00:21:06,654
Wait, are you serious?

272
00:21:06,900 --> 00:21:09,920
All you did was give me
a love tap on the leg.

273
00:21:10,120 --> 00:21:12,600
And you ripped my 20,000 yen pants.

274
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:18,340
For the life of me, I can't figure out
why you Joestars are so stubborn. Fine.

275
00:21:18,640 --> 00:21:20,875
I shall accept your cheap provocation.

276
00:21:21,080 --> 00:21:22,760
Let our comparison resume.

277
00:21:29,380 --> 00:21:37,463
Hoorah!

278
00:21:39,340 --> 00:21:41,046
Comparing our punching speed?

279
00:21:44,200 --> 00:21:45,920
Hoorah! Hoorah! Hoorah!

280
00:22:34,440 --> 00:22:35,270
Thank you.

281
00:23:02,140 --> 00:23:03,880
Thank you.

282
00:23:26,720 --> 00:23:31,140
It's been six months since I began
to grasp the art of stopping time.

283
00:23:31,760 --> 00:23:36,560
And for a moment, it looked as
though time itself had stood still.

284
00:23:37,340 --> 00:23:40,780
The world grind to a halt!
